# Throwing exceptions & custom types

## `throw` — fail fast at the boundary

```java
void setAge(int age) {
    if (age < 0)
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("age >= 0, got " + age);
    this.age = age;
}
```

Reject bad input *where it enters*, value in the message. Prefer the standard types: `IllegalArgumentException`, `IllegalStateException`, `Objects.requireNonNull(x, "x")`.

## Define a custom type — when the failure is domain-meaningful

```java
class OrderNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {   // unchecked: a bug
    OrderNotFoundException(String id) { super("no order " + id); }
}
class InsufficientFundsException extends Exception {      // checked: recoverable
    final BigDecimal shortfall;   // carry data handlers can act on
}
```

- **Pass a message to `super`** — self-explanatory stack trace

## The defining choice

`RuntimeException` → a **bug** (default) · `Exception` → a **recoverable** condition callers must confront (use sparingly).
